<!--
  Workspace Documentation — ArchitectureOverview
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.docgen.workspace.documentation.ArchitectureOverview
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:docgen="org.blockml.bml.docgen"
  xmlns:dcore="org.blockml.bml.docgen.core"
  xmlns:dplan="org.blockml.bml.docgen.plan"
  xmlns:stage="org.blockml.bml.docgen.stage"
  xmlns:bmldocs="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs"
  xmlns:docset="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.docset"
  xmlns:wsdocumentation="org.blockml.bml.docgen.workspace.documentation">

  <name>ArchitectureOverview</name>
  <type>wsdocumentation:ArchitectureOverview</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>How @blockml/docgen and @blockml/bmldocs compose</is>

  <documentation>
    Two layers, one pipeline.

    org.blockml.bml.docgen is the reusable layer. dcore:DocElement is the semantic
    base. A dcore:DocSet owns pages (via pageMapping), a root PageGroup tree, a
    dplan:DocSetPlan, global rules, and authoritativeSources. Pages and groups are
    structural; PageElements (Section, Paragraph, List, Navigation, CodeBlock, …)
    carry content. PageType, ContentRole, DetailLevel, Weight, and SemanticAnnotation
    classify that content. dcore:Rule names generation and authoring constraints.

    Manifestation is staged, not a single compile step:

    1. stage:DocSetPlanningStage — create or update a dplan:DocSetPlan (root
       PageGroupPlan tree of PageGroupPlan / PagePlan; authoritativeSources).
    2. stage:DocSetStructuringStage — materialize or synchronize a concrete DocSet,
       Pages, PageGroups, and pageMapping from that plan.
    3. stage:PageAuthoringStage — author the semantic BML model of each Page
       (structure, roles, annotations, small structural values).
    4. stage:PageRenderingStage — resolve authoritativeSources and emit the target
       manifestation (for example JSON or HTML).

    org.blockml.bml.bmldocs is the site layer. docset:BmlDocSet extends dcore:DocSet
    for BlockML core documentation on blockml.org (rootPath /docs, homePage
    TableOfContents, rootPageGroup RootPageGroup). Concrete pages extend
    docset:BmlDocPage and point at bml-core narrative Blocks. Site rules specialize
    dcore:Rule. bmldocs does not re-implement docgen types.

    The workspace hub orients the monorepo. It does not own DocSets, stages, or
    generation capabilities.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="wsdocumentation:ReadingOrder" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="dcore:DocElement" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="dcore:DocSet" relation="SeeAlso" />
